.Dd $Mdocdate: August 2 2026 $
.Dt Fugu::Proxy 3p
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm Fugu::Proxy ,
.Nm Fugu::Proxy::Cache ,
.Nm Fugu::Proxy::Meta
.Nd a caching HTTP proxy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal
use Fugu::Proxy;

my $cache = Fugu::Proxy::Cache->new(
    dir       => "$ENV{HOME}/.cache/myapp",
    cacheable => sub ($url) { $url =~ m{/pub/.*\e.tgz$} },
);

my $proxy = Fugu::Proxy->new(
    cache   => $cache,
    pidfile => Fugu::Pidfile->new(path => "$dir/proxy.pid"),
    store   => Fugu::Store->new(path => "$dir/state.json")->load,
    child   => 'MyApp::Proxy',
);

my $port = $proxy->start or die $proxy->error . "\en";
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This file holds three packages.
.Nm Fugu::Proxy
is the supervisor and the serve loop.
.Nm Fugu::Proxy::Cache
is the URL-to-file store.
.Nm Fugu::Proxy::Meta
is the metadata that makes a cache hit one write instead of a read and
a re-encode.
.Pp
Nothing here knows what content is worth caching.
That is a callback on the cache, because the answer is a property of
the mirror and not of HTTP.
.Pp
.Xr HTTP::Daemon 3p
and
.Xr LWP::UserAgent 3p
load in the child, at serve time.
Thus the module keeps the core-Perl load contract of Fugu, and an
installation without them still loads it.
.Sh THE SUPERVISOR
.Ss new
.Fn new "%args"
creates a supervisor.
.Pp
These are the arguments:
.Bl -tag -width "logfileXX"
.It Fa cache
A
.Nm Fugu::Proxy::Cache .
This argument is necessary.
.It Fa pidfile
A
.Xr Fugu::Pidfile 3p
for the child.
This argument is necessary.
.It Fa store
A
.Xr Fugu::Store 3p
that holds the port.
This argument is necessary.
.It Fa child
The class whose
.Fn run_child
the spawned child calls.
The default is the class of the supervisor.
.It Fa logfile
Where the output of the child goes.
The default is
.Pa /dev/null .
.It Fa ports
The range to look in, as
.Bq Fa first , Fa last .
The default is 8080 to 8180.
.It Fa log
The logger.
.El
.Ss start
.Fn start
finds a free port, spawns the child, records its PID and port, and
waits until it takes connections.
A proxy that already runs returns its port and starts nothing.
.Ss stop
.Fn stop
stops the child and forgets its port.
The stop is a
.Dv SIGTERM
with a grace period, then a
.Dv SIGKILL ,
through
.Xr Fugu::Process 3p .
.Ss is_running
.Fn is_running
reports if the child is alive.
The check reaps, so a child that became a zombie reads as stopped.
.Ss port , host_url
.Fn port
returns the port the running proxy listens on.
.Fn host_url
returns the URL that reaches it from this machine.
.Ss wait_ready
.Fn wait_ready "$timeout"
polls until the proxy takes a connection.
The default timeout is 30 seconds.
.Ss serve
.Fn serve "$port"
runs the server loop.
The spawned child calls this, and it returns when a
.Dv SIGTERM
arrives.
.Pp
The signal handler writes one byte to a self-pipe that the select loop
watches.
Thus the loop notices the signal between requests and not inside one.
.Ss warm
.Fn warm
fills the metadata table from what is already on disk.
A cold proxy would otherwise stat every file on its first hit.
.Ss cache , error
.Fn cache
returns the cache object.
.Fn error
returns the most recent failure.
.Sh THE CACHE
.Ss new
.Fn new "%args"
creates a cache.
.Pp
These are the arguments:
.Bl -tag -width "cacheableXX"
.It Fa dir
The cache root.
This argument is necessary.
The mirrored tree goes under
.Pa <dir>/proxy .
.It Fa cacheable
A code reference that takes a URL and reports if it is worth keeping.
The default says no.
A cache that guesses fills a home directory with pages nobody will
read again.
.It Fa types
Extra content types, as a hash reference of pattern to type.
.El
.Ss cache_path
.Fn cache_path "$url"
maps a URL to its file:
.Pa <dir>/proxy/<host>/<path> .
The layout is the URL, so a person can find a file and a mirror tree
survives a restart.
.Pp
The method returns
.Dv undef
for a URL that would escape the cache root: no host, an empty path, or
a path that walks up.
A URL comes from a client, so that check is the boundary.
.Ss is_cacheable
.Fn is_cacheable "$url" "$status"
asks the callback.
Only a status of 200 is a candidate: a cached 404 is a mirror that
stays broken after the upstream is fixed.
.Ss lookup , store , store_from_file
.Fn lookup "$url"
returns the cached file, or
.Dv undef .
.Pp
.Fn store "$url" "$content"
writes the content and returns the path.
The write is atomic, so a client that reads while another writes never
gets a partial file.
.Pp
.Fn store_from_file "$url" "$source"
puts a file that is already on disk into the cache.
.Ss size , list , clear
.Fn size
returns the total bytes.
.Fn list
returns every cached file as
.Va url ,
.Va path
and
.Va size .
.Fn clear
removes them all and leaves the root.
.Ss content_type , path_to_url , dir_size , walk
.Fn content_type "$path"
returns the type from the table.
.Fn path_to_url "$path"
rebuilds the URL a cached file came from.
.Fn dir_size "$dir"
returns the bytes under a directory.
.Fn walk "$dir" "$callback"
calls the callback for every regular file under a directory.
One walker serves the size, the listing and the metadata warm.
.Sh THE METADATA
.Ss new , store , lookup
.Fn new
creates an empty table.
.Pp
.Fn store "$url" "$path" "$cache"
builds the entry: the path, the size, the modification time, the
content type and an ETag.
The
.Fa $cache
argument names the content type; without it the type is
.Ql application/octet-stream .
.Pp
.Fn lookup "$url"
returns the entry, or
.Dv undef .
An entry whose file is gone, or whose size or modification time
changed, is not valid and reads as absent.
Thus a file that changed under the proxy invalidates its own entry.
.Ss remove , clear , count , warm
.Fn remove "$url"
forgets one URL.
.Fn clear
forgets them all.
.Fn count
returns the number of entries.
.Fn warm "$cache"
builds an entry for every file already in the cache and returns the
count.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn start
returns the port, or
.Dv undef
with the reason in
.Fn error .
.Fn stop
and
.Fn serve
return 1.
.Fn is_running
and
.Fn wait_ready
return 1 or 0.
.Pp
.Fn store
and
.Fn cache_path
return a path, or
.Dv undef .
.Fn list
returns an array reference.
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn new
dies when a necessary argument is absent.
.Fn serve
dies when
.Xr HTTP::Daemon 3p
is missing, and when it cannot listen.
Both are startup failures of a child that exists to serve.
.Pp
No other method dies.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr Fugu::File 3p ,
.Xr Fugu::Pidfile 3p ,
.Xr Fugu::Process 3p ,
.Xr Fugu::Store 3p ,
.Xr HTTP::Daemon 3p ,
.Xr LWP::UserAgent 3p
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Dick Olsson Aq Mt hi@senzilla.io
.Sh CAVEATS
The cache has no bound of its own and no expiry.
Nothing removes an entry until the caller does.
A caller whose URLs are version-scoped prunes by version; a caller
whose URLs are not needs a policy that this module does not have.
.Pp
The serve loop handles one client at a time.
A large transfer therefore holds the proxy.
That is the right trade for a mirror that one machine reads.
